# .envrc — cv-main (OPTIONAL, direnv users only)
#
# - You do NOT use direnv: this file is totally ignored by the shell (zero effect).
# - You use direnv: run `direnv allow` once.
#
# What happens on cd into this repo:
#   * Exports per-project FPATH to ./completions (for zsh).
# For full TAB support you still need ONCE (zsh+bash):
#   ./completions/install.sh
#
# Why is the installer still needed? direnv limitation: it only forwards
# environment variables to the parent shell, not completion functions or
# `complete`/`compdef` registrations. So .envrc = automatic per-project FPATH,
# install.sh = completion registration.
#
# Nix users (optional): this file is intentionally nix-agnostic.
# Enter the reproducible environment manually with `nix develop`
# (flakes) or `nix-shell` (classic), then use ./compile.sh as usual.

if has expand_path 2>/dev/null; then
  # shellcheck disable=SC2155
  export FPATH="$(expand_path ./completions):${FPATH:-}"
fi
